      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because basenames never contain `/`, `ix.baseMatchesFrom(i, 0)` is always `false` whenever the query contains a `/`. For any path-qualified query, `scoreFrom` therefore falls back to `dm[ix.dirId[i]]`, where greedy directory matching across deeper directory segments can consume the leading characters of the filename portion even when the basename carries the entire post-slash query on its own:\n\n- Querying `java/gitilesview` against `java/com/google/gitiles/{GitilesView,ViewFilter}.java`: the directory `java/com/google/gitiles` greedily consumes `java/gitiles` (`dm[d] \u003d 12`), leaving only `view` for `scoreBasename`. That matches at index `0` of `ViewFilter.java` (earning `BONUS_START \u003d 40`) vs. index `7` of `GitilesView.java`, ranking `ViewFilter.java` above `GitilesView.java`.\n- Querying `net/base64.h` against `net/base/{64.h,base64.h}`: the directory `net/base` consumes `net/base`, ranking `net/base/64.h` above `net/base/base64.h` and highlighting `net/base/base64.h` as `\u003cmark\u003enet/base\u003c/mark\u003e/base\u003cmark\u003e64.h\u003c/mark\u003e` instead of `\u003cmark\u003enet/\u003c/mark\u003ebase/\u003cmark\u003ebase64.h\u003c/mark\u003e`.\n- Querying `java/gitiles`: `java/com/google/gitiles/GitilesServlet.java` has all of `java/gitiles` consumed by its directory (`from \u003d 12 \u003d\u003d\u003d q.length`), giving it `scoreBasename \u003d 0` and ranking `BlameServlet.java` ahead of `GitilesServlet.java`.\n\nSince every candidate returned by `narrowD` already satisfies `dm[ix.dirId[i]] \u003e\u003d ix.q.lastIndexOf(SLASH) + 1`, checking whether the basename matches starting right after the last `/` (`0` when the query has no `/`) preserves the slash-free behavior while preventing deeper directories from stealing characters from a basename that matches the full filename portion of the query:\n\n```suggestion\nfunction scoreFrom(ix, dm, i) {\n  const minFrom \u003d ix.q.lastIndexOf(SLASH) + 1;\n  return ix.baseMatchesFrom(i, minFrom) ? minFrom : dm[ix.dirId[i]];\n}\n```\n\n_from potto_",
