      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: In Channels C (here) and D (line 991), shifting `ix.staticRank[i] \u003e\u003e 4` discards the low 4 bits of `staticRank`, collapsing path-length and depth differences of up to 15 points into the same bucket (where `TopK` ties fall back to lexicographic index order). For example, on a Channel C query like `lutil`, `a/b/logging_util.h` (`depth \u003d 2`, `staticRank \u003d -41`, `-41 \u003e\u003e 4 \u003d\u003d\u003d -3`) and `content/logging_util.h` (`depth \u003d 1`, `staticRank \u003d -33`, `-33 \u003e\u003e 4 \u003d\u003d\u003d -3`) tie and `a/b/logging_util.h` ranks first solely because `\"a/b\"` sorts before `\"content\"`.\n\nSince `TopK.score` is already a `Float64Array`, scaling `sc` by `1024` instead of right-shifting `staticRank` by `4` (and using `1 \u003c\u003c 24` for the directory penalty on line 991) keeps the exact same `1024:1` relative weight between `sc` and `staticRank` while preserving full tie-breaker precision:\n\n```suggestion\n      const sc \u003d scoreBasename(ix, i, 0);\n      top.offer(sc * 1024 + ix.staticRank[i], i);\n    }\n```\n\n_from potto_",
