      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T21:13:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the user opens the finder (or clears the input) and `recentPaths()` is non-empty, `query()` sends `{type: \u0027recent\u0027, ...}` instead of `{type: \u0027query\u0027, q: \u0027\u0027}`. In the worker, the `recent` handler filters `msg.paths` against `index.indexOfPath(p)` so deleted or branch-specific files do not 404.\n\nHowever, if *none* of the remembered paths in `localStorage` exist at the currently viewed revision (for example, the user previously opened files on another branch/CL or files that have since been renamed/deleted), the worker responds with `{type: \u0027results\u0027, ..., recent: true, items: []}`, and `render([], 0, true)` leaves the palette completely blank (`0` visible rows and an empty status label) instead of falling back to the ordinary tree listing.\n\nIf a `recent` lookup resolves to zero existing files in the current tree, falling back to the normal empty-query search avoids showing an empty palette:\n\n```suggestion\n        // Ignore responses overtaken by later keystrokes.\n        if (msg.seq \u003d\u003d\u003d seq) {\n          if (showingRecent \u0026\u0026 !msg.items.length) {\n            showingRecent \u003d false;\n            seq++;\n            worker.postMessage({type: \u0027query\u0027, seq: seq, q: input.value});\n            return;\n          }\n          render(msg.items, msg.total, msg.exact);\n        }\n```\n\n_from potto_",
